 "narration": [
  "Same building. Same AC. So why is your flat so much hotter than your neighbour's?",
  "First, the sun. West-facing flats take the harshest sun in the afternoon, right when the day is hottest.",
  "Second, the glass. Big, unshaded windows let the heat straight in. Clear glass with no shade is the worst combination.",
  "Third, the roof. Top-floor flats sit under a slab that bakes all day and gives that heat back all night.",
  "Fourth, the walls. Thin walls with no insulation pass the outside heat straight into your living room.",
  "The fixes are simpler than you think. Shade the west windows from outside, add a white reflective roof coating, and run the ceiling fan before the AC.",
  "Green buildings solve this on paper, before anyone moves in. So before you buy, ask which way the flat faces."
 ],
